[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1119,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 1158,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 156425,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 1158,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Papillary intralymphatic angioendothelioma (PILA) is an uncommon, rarely metastasizing, superficial lymphatic vascular tumour, showing tufting and hobnail endothelial proliferations within lymphatic channel lumina, in a background of lymphatic vascular proliferation or lymphangioma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-09-01T10:19:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1120,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 1159,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 156426,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 1159,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9135/1 Papillary intralymphatic angioendothelioma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-09-01T10:19:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1121,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 1160,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 156427,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 1160,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F72.Y &amp; XH4SY7 Other specified neoplasms of uncertain behaviour of skin &amp; papillary intralymphatic angioendothelioma of unspecified site.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-09-01T10:19:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1122,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 1161,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 156428,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 1161,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> Dabska tumour; endovascular papillary angioendothelioma; hobnail haemangioendothelioma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-09-01T10:19:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1123,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 1162,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 156429,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 1162,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not defined.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-09-01T10:19:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1124,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 1163,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 156430,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 1163,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most PILAs involve the proximal extremities, especially the buttock or thigh, and less commonly the distal extremities or trunk, head and neck, intra-abdominal sites, or parenchymal sites (including testis) {3444784; 8522288; 21695802; 10971050}. Intraosseous locations are rarely reported {10478659; 10197456; 24063649; 29423171}. Some arise in association with pre-existing vascular malformations&nbsp;/ lymphatic anomalies {9302935;8806966; 5343389}, including lymphangioma circumscriptum {18095998}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-09-01T10:19:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1125,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 1164,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 156431,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 1164,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is a slight female predilection (M:F&nbsp;ratio: ~0.7:1). PILA presents as a slow-growing asymptomatic cutaneous induration, plaque, or rarely nodule, often with unremarkable overlying skin.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-09-01T10:19:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1126,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 1165,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 156432,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 1165,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>PILA is exceedingly rare, with &lt;&nbsp;50&nbsp;reported cases {5343389; 10478659; 32151408}. It is difficult to estimate the exact incidence of this tumour, as a considerable percentage of reported cases appear instead to represent papillary endothelial hyperplasia, angiosarcoma with papillary growth, and lymphatic malformations with papillary endothelial proliferation {38497350}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-09-01T10:19:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1127,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 1166,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 156433,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 1166,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-09-01T10:19:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1128,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 1167,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 156434,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 1167,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-09-01T10:19:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1135,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 1174,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 156435,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 1174,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are poorly defined and usually involve dermis and subcutaneous tissue {10478659}. Grossly, greyish-white to pink streaks or cystic change in otherwise normal dermis and subcutis may be present, without haemorrhage or necrosis. Tumour size ranges from 10&nbsp;to &gt;&nbsp;400&nbsp;mm (mean: 70&nbsp;mm) {10478659}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-09-01T10:19:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1129,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 1168,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 156436,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 1168,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>PILA is a poorly delineated dermal and/or subcutaneous proliferation of lymphatic channels showing variable intraluminal papillary tuft proliferation, with hyaline cores and intermixed lymphocytes with proteinaceous fluid. A lymphatic vascular malformation is often present nearby. The cavernous or slit-like lymphatic vascular channels are lined by columnar, matchstick-like, or hobnail endothelial cells. The lesional cells have eosinophilic cytoplasm and round uniform nuclei with indistinct nucleoli; they lack cytological atypia and mitoses {10478659}. Tumour cells express panendothelial markers, such as CD31, ERG, and less often CD34, as well as lymphatic endothelial markers, such as podoplanin, VEGFR3, and PROX1 {10478659; 22067331; 10971050}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-09-01T10:19:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1130,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 1169,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 156437,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 1169,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Insufficient data</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-09-01T10:19:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1131,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 1170,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 156438,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 1170,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-09-01T10:19:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1134,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 1173,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 156439,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 1173,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> poorly defined lymphatic vessels with stromal and intraluminal lymphocytes and proteinaceous fluid; intralymphatic, intraluminal hobnail proliferation of polarized matchstick-like columnar endothelial cells; expression of panendothelial and lymphatic markers.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-09-01T10:19:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1132,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 1171,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 156440,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 1171,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-09-01T10:19:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1133,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 1172,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 156441,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 1172,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most patients have excellent prognosis after complete excision {10478659}. Lymph node metastases are extremely rare, and only a single death from disease has been reported {5343389; 9302935}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-09-01T10:19:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]